7.What is the purpose of background-clip: content-box;?

Colors, Background & Typography • Level: Hard

A)It clips the image to the border
B)It clips the image to the padding
C)It clips the image to the content area only
D)It removes the image


✅ Correct Answer: C) It clips the image to the content area only

Simple English:

background-clip: content-box; means the background is shown only inside the content area.

It does not appear in the padding or border.

Example:
.box {
  background: lightblue;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 5px solid black;
  background-clip: content-box;
}

👉 The light blue background is visible only in the content area.

Easy Remember:
content-box → Background only in content
padding-box → Background in content + padding
border-box → Background in content + padding + border (default)
Options:
❌ A) It clips the image to the border
❌ B) It clips the image to the padding
✅ C) It clips the image to the content area only
❌ D) It removes the image

✅ Final Answer: C) It clips the image to the content area only

